ner tall">", "-    <canvas id="weeklyTrendChart"></canvas>", "-  </div>", "+  <p>Global average retail prices track Brent Crude with high fidelity. At the weekly global-average level, the correlation is r = <span class="hl">{round(r_weekly_petrol, 3)}</span> for petrol and r = <span class="hl">{round(r_weekly_diesel, 3)}</span> for diesel (both p &lt; 0.001). Week-over-week changes in Brent explain {round(r_fd_petrol**2 * 100, 1)}% of the variance in weekly retail petrol changes (first-difference r = {round(r_fd_petrol, 3)}).</p>", "+  <p>At the individual country level, the mean within-country Brent–petrol correlation is <span class="hl">r = {mean_country_corr}</span> (median r = {median_country_corr}), and the mean first-difference correlation is <span class="hl">r = {mean_country_fd_corr}</span> (median r = {median_country_fd_corr}). The gap between level and first-difference correlations indicates that while countries share the same long-run trend, short-term pass-through varies considerably — a key finding for subsidy analysis.</p>", " ", "+  <div class="chart tall"><canvas id="weeklyTrendChart"></canvas></div>", "+", "   <h3>2.2 Yearly Average Prices</h3>", "   <table>", "     <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Petrol (USD/L)</th><th>Diesel (USD/L)</th><th>LPG (USD/L)</th><th>Brent Crude (USD/bbl)</th></tr></thead>"]}, {"oldStart": 481, "oldLines": 181, "newStart": 366, "newLines": 164, "lines": [" """", " ", " for _, row in yearly_avg.iterrows():", "-    html += f"""      <tr><td>{int(row['year'])}</td><td>${row['petrol_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['diesel_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['lpg_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['brent_crude_usd']}</td></tr>\n"""", "+    html += f"      <tr><td>{int(row['year'])}</td><td>${row['petrol_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['diesel_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['lpg_usd_liter']}</td><td>${row['brent_crude_usd']}</td></tr>\n"", " ", " html += f"""    </tbody>", "   </table>", " ", "   <h3>2.3 Crisis Period Analysis</h3>", "   <div class="kpi-grid">", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="value">{covid_brent_drop}%</div>", "-      <div class="label">Brent Crude Drop (COVID)</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="value">{covid_petrol_drop}%</div>", "-      <div class="label">Petrol Price Drop (COVID)</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="value">${crisis_avg_brent}</div>", "-      <div class="label">Avg Brent 2022 Crisis</div>", "-    </div>", "-    <div class="kpi-card">", "-      <div class="value">${crisis_avg_petrol}</div>", "-      <div class="label">Avg Petrol 2022 Crisis</div>", "-    </div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="val">{covid_brent_drop}%</div><div class="lbl">Brent Crude Drop (COVID)</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="val">{covid_petrol_drop}%</div><div class="lbl">Petrol Price Drop (COVID)</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="val">${crisis_b}</div><div class="lbl">Avg Brent 2022 Crisis</div></div>", "+    <div class="kpi-card"><div class="val">${crisis_p}</div><div class="lbl">Avg Petrol 2022 Crisis</div></div>", "   </div>", "-  <p>During the COVID-19 demand shock (Mar–Jun 2020), Brent Crude fell <span class="neg">{covid_brent_drop}%</span> from its pre-pandemic baseline (${pre_covid_brent} → ${covid_avg_brent} USD/bbl), while retail petrol dropped a more muted <span class="neg">{covid_petrol_drop}%</span> (${pre_covid_petrol} → ${covid_avg_petrol} USD/L). The asymmetric pass-through — where crude fell faster than retail — reflects the dampening effect of fixed taxes and subsidies that insulate pump prices from commodity swings.</p>", "-  <p>During the 2022 energy crisis, Brent Crude averaged ${crisis_avg_brent} USD/bbl and petrol averaged ${crisis_avg_petrol} USD/L globally, the highest annual averages in the dataset.</p>", "+  <p>During the COVID-19 demand shock (Mar–Jun 2020), Brent Crude fell <span class="neg">{covid_brent_drop}%</span> from its pre-pandemic baseline (${pre_covid_b} &rarr; ${covid_b} USD/bbl), while retail petrol dropped a more muted <span class="neg">{covid_petrol_drop}%</span> (${pre_covid_p} &rarr; ${covid_p} USD/L). The asymmetric pass-through — where crude fell faster than retail — reflects the floor effect of fixed taxes and subsidies that insulate pump prices from commodity swings.</p>", "+  <p>During the 2022 energy crisis, Brent Crude averaged ${crisis_b} USD/bbl and petrol averaged ${crisis_p} USD/L globally — the highest annual averages in the dataset, placing severe pressure on consumers in unsubsidized markets.</p>", " ", "   <h3>2.4 Volatility by Year (Coefficient of Variation)</h3>", "-  <div class="chart-container short">", "-    <canvas id="volatilityChart"></canvas>", "-  </div>", "+  <div class="chart med"><canvas id="volatilityChart"></canvas></div>", "   <table>", "     <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Petrol CV</th><th>Diesel CV</th><th>LPG CV</th></tr></thead>", "     <tbody>", " """", " ", "-for _, row in yearly_volatility.iterrows():", "-    html += f"""      <tr><td>{int(row['year'])}</td><td>{row['petrol_cv']:.2%}</td><td>{row['diesel_cv']:.2%}</td><td>{row['lpg_cv']:.2%}</td></tr>\n"""", "+for _, row in yearly_vol.iterrows():", "+    html += f"      <tr><td>{int(row['year'])}</td><td>{row['petrol_cv']:.2%}</td><td>{row['diesel_cv']:.2%}</td><td>{row['lpg_cv']:.2%}</td></tr>\n"", " ", " html += f"""    </tbody>", "   </table>", "-  <p>Cross-country price dispersion (CV) peaked during 2020 as nations diverged in their COVID response, and again in 2022 when subsidy regimes produced starkly different outcomes across economies.</p>", "+  <p>Cross-country price dispersion (CV) peaked during 2020 as nations diverged in their COVID-19 response, and again during the 2022 crisis when subsidy regimes produced starkly different outcomes across economies.</p>", " ", "-  <h3>2.5 Brent-to-Retail Correlation</h3>", "+  <h3>2.5 Brent-to-Retail Correlation Summary</h3>", "   <table>", "-    <thead><tr>